<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| sim event -> session state | the death event changes what the session may do next (save, pause, input) |
| session -> IndexedDB | a snapshot crosses into durable storage; a dead state must never cross |
| `?test=1` hook -> session | a page script can drive the session; it must not produce a dead save |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-20-10 | Tampering | overwriting the last good save with a dead or "docked" player | high | mitigate | the latch first in `autosave`/`manualSave`/`writeManualSave`; `buildSnapshotInputs`/`queueSnapshot` refusal; `snapshotForSave` throws on `"dead"` (20-01, in the death commit); the schema cannot encode it; same-frame and pending-write tests |
| T-20-11 | Tampering | a missing `deathFlow` in some construction path leaving the session unlatched | medium | mitigate | the router installs `createDeathFlow(ctx)` when none is supplied; a test dispatches through a router built without one |
| T-20-12 | Elevation of privilege | input reaching the flight controller or station screens after death | medium | mitigate | `gameOver` input context with no action; input cleared at the latch; 20-06 drains every queue in the frame loop |
| T-20-13 | Tampering | HTML injection through a culprit name | low | transfer | names are rendered by 20-05 with `textContent` only; this plan passes the cause as data |
| T-20-36 | Denial of service | the player's eight bursts overwriting a same-tick NPC explosion (D-09) in a pool of 8, or a seed or burst-kind change altering every Phase 16 explosion | low | mitigate | the pool grows to 16 with a nine-live-explosions test; variant 0 or no options keeps today's seed string and today's cloud parameters (no kind), pinned by the existing Phase 16 cases, the identical-particles case included; two draw objects pinned for 16 and 50 adds |
| T-20-41 | Tampering | `loadFromSave` or `clearSaveForNewGame` replacing or clearing the save after a death, or a late completion hiding the `dead` refusal | medium | mitigate | both return first while latched (Task 2 tests); the completion keeps `saveSkipReason` at `dead` while latched |
| T-20-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | low | accept | no package is installed or changed |
</threat_model>

