<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| session state -> window probe | the probe is read by page scripts (`?test=1` specs) |
| render -> sim | the render driver must not write sim state |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-20-23 | Information disclosure | `probe.death.cause` exposing an entity id | low | mitigate | the cause holds a key string only; `tests/guards/entity-id-scope.test.ts` stays green |
| T-20-24 | Tampering | the presentation clock or the debris drift leaking into the sim or the hash | medium | mitigate | `gameOverSeconds` is read only by render and frame code; the effect time is passed to render layers only; the drift moves copied contacts, never an entity (Task 2 pins `hashWorld`, `hashFlight` and every debris entity unchanged across dead frames); 20-03 pins the dead hash |
| T-20-25 | Denial of service | a CSS filter or redraw loop costing frames forever | low | mitigate | the filter is written only on change and cleared when not dead; drawing settles after the fade and the burst lifetimes, and keeps going after that only while debris moves on screen (D-01c), at the per-frame cost of flight |
| T-20-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | low | accept | no package is installed or changed |
</threat_model>

