[0m⚙ [0mcompress {"topic":"Phase 20 fidelity review evidence","content":[{"startId":"@3@","endId":"@27@","summary":"REVIEW TASK (from the user prompt, keep in mind): read-only fidelity review of Wegolite Phase 20 owner decisions DIV-9 (one flash, D-01b), DIV-2 updated (explosion particle form only, D-01a) and DIV-7 updated (frozen sim, moving presentation layers, D-01c). Verify against Oolite pin 7437f22 (`git -C /home/opencode/git/oolite show 7437f22:<path>`) and the plans 20-04/20-08/20-10; output markdown only: up to five short implementation concerns citing path:line, then exactly three lines in the form `- DIV-9 (one flash): ACCEPT | OBJECT — ...` etc. Repo /home/opencode/git/wegolite. Review round 1 commit is 4e28360; planning baseline a5a03ce; 20-REVIEWS.md (950 lines) holds DIV-1..DIV-8 verdicts from Fable/Sonnet/Kimi but no DIV-9 verdict yet (this review supplies it; 20-10 halts without explicit DIV-9 verdicts). No code has been written yet (only docs commits).\n\nPHASE CONTEXT DECISIONS (20-CONTEXT.md): D-01 as amended 2026-11-22: Oolite's `becomeLargeExplosion:4.0` 4.0 is a burst count, not a size; eight Phase 16 clouds on the death tick, four small + four big, distinct seeds, each at 1x the player's collision radius (never x4); only the particle form diverges. D-01a: each kind takes speed range, lifetime and start size from OOParticleSystem.m at the pin (small 100-400 m/s, 1.5 s, start size `32*100/speed`, no growth; big `1+0.5r` up to 4x that, 1.0 s, start size `2r` growing to `(1+t)2r`). D-01b: exactly ONE flash for the whole player explosion, on the first burst (new divergence DIV-9). D-01c: sim frozen at the death tick (deterministic dead hash) but explosions, shots, NPC debris (render-only extrapolation: last sim position + velocity x presentation time) and the B&W fade keep moving; ships, buoys, station, dust stand still. Accepted planner calls: explosion pool 8 -> 16; 5 s B&W fade; HUD hidden, messages cleared; QUAL-11's collision kill is the nav buoy destroyed by the same ram.\n\n20-04-PLAN.md (wave 2, app/session + render): Task 1 adds `SessionRuntime.gameOver/.gameOverSeconds/.gameOverCause`, `latchGameOver(ctx, cause)`, `createDeathFlow` as seventh subscriber, routes `playerDestroyed` (24 -> 25 kinds), save skip reason `\"dead\"` ahead of every save guard. Task 2 refuses `writeManualSave`, `buildSnapshotInputs`, `queueSnapshot`, `loadFromSave`, `clearSaveForNewGame` while latched; keeps `saveSkipReason` `dead` when a late pre-death write completes; adds `InputContext \"gameOver\"` with no action (F1-F8 swallowed). Task 3: `ExplosionLayer.add` gains `ExplosionAddOptions {variant?, flash?, kind?}`, `ExplosionBurstKind = \"small\"|\"big\"`, nine constants `SMALL_BURST_MIN_SPEED=100`, `SMALL_BURST_MAX_SPEED=400`, `SMALL_BURST_DURATION=1.5`, `SMALL_BURST_SIZE_FACTOR=32`, `BIG_BURST_MIN_SPEED_BASE=1`, `BIG_BURST_MIN_SPEED_PER_RADIUS=0.5`, `BIG_BURST_SPEED_SPAN=4`, `BIG_BURST_SIZE_FACTOR=2`, `BIG_BURST_DURATION=1`; per-particle start-size array beside `speed` used in the quad edge `2*(start+growth*t)`; no-kind path byte-identical to today (same seed string `${x},${y},${z},${radius}`, same draw order); variant appended as `,${variant}` when non-zero; per-slot flash flag; `EXPLOSION_POOL` 8 -> 16; `PLAYER_EXPLOSION_FACTOR = 4`; `PLAYER_EXPLOSION_SETTINGS` = copy of the generated `oolite-default-ship-explosion` record minus `key`, frozen (defensive with traffic off); death flow closes chart + F2 screen, `setContext(\"gameOver\")`, `messages.clear()`, `launchSequence.reset()`, `hudCanvas.hidden = true`, then `2*PLAYER_EXPLOSION_FACTOR = 8` adds at the event position with radius `PLAYER_COLLISION_RADIUS_M` (72.69734954833984), k=1..4 kind `small`, k=5..8 kind `big`, `variant: k`, `flash: true` for k=1 only. Tests assert exactly one player flash, pool 16, variant distinctness, per-kind speed/lifetime/size, hash untouched.\n\n20-08-PLAN.md (wave 4): Task 1 exports `GAME_OVER_FADE_SECONDS = 5` (Oolite's `gameover-seconds-to-bw-fadeout` default, PlayerEntity.m:3566-3568) and `DEAD_CAMERA_SETBACK_M = 100` (`moveForward:100.0`); dead camera = `computeViewCamera(position + forward*100, orientation, \"aft\", zero)`; effect time `flightTime + gameOverSeconds` passed to `shots.update` and `explosions.update` (alive they are equal); `previousCameraWorld` cleared on the first dead frame so dust gets a zero delta; `data-dead` attribute; `hudHidden` true for dead; canvas `filter: saturate(1 - min(1, gameOverSeconds/5))` written only on change (first frame always writes) and the same string to `ctx.runtime.gameOverOverlay?.setFilter`; `shouldDraw` keeps drawing while latched and `gameOverSeconds` below the settle time = max(5, SMALL_BURST_DURATION, BIG_BURST_DURATION). Task 2 (D-01c): `DebrisContact` gains a copied `velocity`; while latched the driver maps contacts to position + velocity*gameOverSeconds in float64 and passes `flightTime + gameOverSeconds` to `debris.update` (tumble); `hashWorld`/`hashFlight` and every debris entity pinned unchanged across dead frames; `shouldDraw` stays true past the settle time while any debris contact has non-zero velocity (flag cached from the last frame's contacts); only `src/sim/world/contacts.ts` may change under the QUAL-11 trigger paths; `src/render/bodies/debris.ts` untouched. Task 3 publishes `probe.death` from `gameOverCause`.\n\n20-10-PLAN.md (wave 6, close-out): PROJECT.md Key Decisions amendments (energy floor, collisions, explosions-and-debris row: pool 16, variant/kind/no-flash adds, eight bursts with one flash, dead debris drawn moved by velocity), four new rows (playerDestroyed payload; reload + latch; game-over view; dead presentation); FIDELITY rows with <=20-line excerpts copied from the pin; every divergence quotes an exact PROJECT.md substring and names only reviewers with explicit accepting comments; the DIV-9 row's Oolite cell is `src/Core/Entities/ShipEntity.m:8308-8320`, sharing the explosion row's excerpt, its Wegolite cell is the `flash` option line in `src/app/session/event-router.ts`, and (must_haves) 'its reason is the owner's decision as 20-CONTEXT.md D-01b records it, with no reason the record does not hold'; the explosion row discloses the particle-count divergence (cloud's 10 vs Oolite's small `0.4 r | 12` up to 64 and big `0.2 r | 3` up to 16, `OOParticleSystem.m:253-254`, `:305-306`), plus colours/alpha/texture, the unmodelled `releaseCargoPodsDebris` (ShipEntity.m:8322), `noteKilledBy:` (PlayerEntity.m:6206) and the absent drift with the ship's velocity; the DIV-7 row lists moving layers (explosions incl. any live at death, shots retiring, debris render-only drifted and tumbling, the fade of scene and text) and still layers (ships, buoys, station, dust); one `e2e-cross` run, remote `verify-full`, 20-seed acceptance 21/21 at phase HEAD; no version bump/tag; the Phase 20 executor brief pins PlayerEntity.m:99 kDeadResetTime, :2450-2453 dead update branch, :3551-3564 performDeadUpdates, :3566-3590 gameOverFadeToBW, :3630-3644 showGameOver, :6187-6221 getDestroyedBy:, PlayerEntityControls.m:4016-4027 pollGameOverControls, Universe.m:2961-2968 handleGameOver, ShipEntity.m:8300-8330 becomeLargeExplosion:, OOParticleSystem.m:244-296 and :298-353, descriptions.plist:1990-1993.\n\nOOLITE SOURCE VERIFIED AT PIN 7437f22: `ShipEntity.m:8300-8320` = `- (void)becomeLargeExplosion:(double)factor`, STATUS_DEAD guard 8303-8305, comment 'two parts to the explosion', small-burst loop 8310-8314 (`how_many = factor; while (how_many > 0.5f) add OOSmallFragmentBurstEntity`), big-burst loop 8316-8320; factor 4.0 -> exactly 4 + 4 adds; NO flash and no cloud; `releaseCargoPodsDebris` 8322. Ordinary explosion default branch `ShipEntity.m:7957-7965`: `OOExplosionCloudEntity` at 7962 plus `OOFlashEffectEntity` at 7964 (the cloud+flash pair, cited in the prompt as 7957-7964); the reduced-detail branch 7945-7953 adds 1 small burst + 1 big burst + 1 flash. `PlayerEntity.m:6187-6223 getDestroyedBy:`: docked-only refusal 6189-6190, `setDisplayText:NO` 6202, `VIEW_AFT` 6203, `noteKilledBy:` 6206, `becomeLargeExplosion:4.0` 6208, `moveForward:100.0` 6209, `flightSpeed = 160`, messageGUI clear 6216, `showGameOver` 6222, `removeAllEquipment` 6220. `kDeadResetTime = 30.0f` at PlayerEntity.m:99. `performDeadUpdates` 3551-3564 (fade, then `[self shotTime] > kDeadResetTime` -> handleGameOver). `gameOverFadeToBW` 3566-3590: 5.0 s default, applied only when `[UNIVERSE detailLevel] >= DETAIL_LEVEL_SHADERS`. `showGameOver` 3630-3644: 3 texts (Game Over, `gameoverscreen-score-@` via `KillCountToRatingAndKillString(ship_kills)`, Press Space) interleaved with blank rows, each for kDeadResetTime, then `resetShotTime`; no pause, no GUI screen switch. PlayerEntity.m:2450-2453 `if (status == STATUS_DEAD) [self performDeadUpdates:delta_t]` inside `update:`. `Universe.m:6421-6426` update runs whenever `!no_update`; 6533-6547 updates every live entity and skips only newly dead non-player entities (comment 6539-6540 'Game Over code depends on regular delta_t updates to the dead player entity'); 6662-6666 the else-branch still calls `[PLAYER update:delta_t]` when dead; `no_update` is set only by reset/draw blocking (4360-4373, 5157-5198, 9376/9474), so Oolite's universe genuinely keeps running through the dead window. `Universe.m:2961-2968 handleGameOver` -> `loadPlayerIfRequired`. `OOParticleSystem.m`: shared init 48-85, speed sampling `minSpeed + 0.5f*(randf()+randf())*(maxSpeed-minSpeed)` at 67, `_particleSize[i] = speed` at 77; small burst 244-296 with kMinSpeed 100 / kMaxSpeed 400 (249-250), count `0.4f*size` with `MIN(count|12, 64)` (253-254), duration 1.5 (262), start size `_particleSize[i] = 32.0f*kMinSpeed/_particleSize[i]` (265), update changes only per-particle alpha `du = 0.5 + (1/32)(32-i)` (no size growth); big burst 298-353 with `minSpeed = 1.0f + size*0.5f` (302), `maxSpeed = minSpeed*4.0f` (303), count `0.2f*size` with `MIN(count|3, 16)` (305-306), baseColor {1,1,0.5,1} (308), `size *= 2.0f` (310), duration 1.0 (311), update size `(1.0f + timePassed)*_baseSize` (342). Enum caps: `kFragmentBurstMaxParticles = 64`, `kBigFragmentBurstMaxParticles = 16` (OOParticleSystem.h:34-35). At the player's r = 72.697 this gives 29 small particles per burst and 14 big, versus Wegolite's 10 per cloud. Big speeds 37.35-149.4 m/s, matching the context's 'about 37-149 m/s'.\n\nWEGOLITE CODE: `src/render/bodies/explosions.ts`: `EXPLOSION_POOL = 8` (105), `EXPLOSION_MAX_PARTICLES = 10` (112), `FLASH_DURATION 0.4` (115), `FLASH_ALPHA 0.5` (118), `FLASH_GROWTH_FACTOR 150` (121), `FLASH_MIN_GROWTH 600` (124), `FLASH_FADE_IN 0.667` (127), `CLOUD_CAPACITY = pool*particles` (184); `add()` 364-451: `size = radius*settings.size` (392), `growthRate = settings.growthRate*size` (399), `duration = settings.duration` (400), `flashSize = radius` (403), `flashGrowth = max(150*radius, 600)` (404-407), seed string `${x},${y},${z},${radius}` (419), speeds `size*0.8*spread` to `size*1.2*spread` (424-425), speed draw `min + 0.5*(u+u)*(max-min)` (428-429), direction (431-436), colours (437-449); textures load lazily on first add (377-384). `update()` 452-540: `t = flightTime - start` (469), `cloudOn = t >= 0 && t < life` (471), `flashOn = t <= FLASH_DURATION` (472), expired slot freed permanently `startTime = NaN` (475-478), flash edge `2*(flashSize + flashGrowth*t)` (486-488), cloud edge `2*(v + growth*t)` where v is the particle speed doubling as start size (522), alpha `cloudAlpha*(1 - t/life)` (504). `src/content/generated/explosions.json` single record: alpha 0.8500000238418579, brightness 1, colorOrder rgb, count 25, duration 1.5, growthRate 1.5, size 2.5, spread 1, texture oolite-particle-cloud2.png (so the ordinary cloud starts particles at 2.5r = 181.7 m growing at 272.6 m/s, i.e. larger and faster-growing than Oolite's big burst at 2r and 2r/s). `src/app/session/render-driver.ts`: `shouldDraw()` 160-165 = `redrawGate.next(paused || frozenDocked, drawKeys())`; camera branches launchView (230-244) and `mode === \"inFlight\"` (245-254); `applyFrame` 255-263; dust update 272-280 using `ctx.core.previousCameraWorld`; hull always `visible = false` (282); `npcContacts` 287, `debrisContacts` 297, `debris.update(..., currentState.flightTime)` 299-305; `shots.update(cameraWorld, currentState.flightTime, pose)` 308-311; `explosions.update(cameraWorld, quaternion, currentState.flightTime)` 315-319; draw block 321-329; message clock `flightTime + dockedMessageSeconds` (339-341); `hudHidden = mode === \"docked\" && !preRolling` (368), `hudCanvas.hidden` (369), `data-launching` toggle (383), HUD draw only `!hudHidden && draw` (384). `tests/contract/fidelity.test.ts`: test 'gives every Oolite citation exactly one excerpt with the same path and range' (222-239) — each row's Excerpt cell must name exactly one excerpt heading, `bare(ooliteCell)` must equal `path:start-end`; two rows MAY share one excerpt ID (8308-8320 is 13 lines, within the 20-line cap); divergences must quote a substring of PROJECT.md (264-274); other tests check the Wegolite `path:line` exists (203-220), excerpt block length == range (241-254), ASSETS row.\n\nCLOSED FINDINGS: The three Oolite claims in the prompt are accurate; DIV-2's burst count/kinds/speeds/lifetimes/start sizes all match the pin; DIV-7's premise that Oolite's universe keeps running through the dead window is confirmed. Remaining candidate concerns: (a) the DIV-9 flash starts at 1x r = 72.7 m and grows at max(150r,600) ~ 10.9 km/s for 0.4 s at a camera only 100 m away (quad ~4.4 km across), so it whites out the frame for ~0.2 s and hides the eight-burst structure, while Oolite's player death has no flash (explosions.ts:404-407, 486-488); (b) the dead settle rule never idles because sim debris drift is constant-velocity, so `shouldDraw` stays true for as long as any piece exists, even off-screen, contradicting T-20-25's 'drawing settles after the fade', and Task 2 allocates a new contact array every dead frame; (c) 20-10 writes the DIV-9 reason as 'the owner's decision ... with no reason the record does not hold', but the fidelity rule requires 'clearly better', so the row should state the clarity reason (a flash marks the moment; Oolite's ordinary explosion has one; four small bursts are dim at 100 m); (d) the DIV-2 line's phrase 'burst counts ... taken from OOParticleSystem.m' conflates the 4+4 burst count from ShipEntity.m:8311-8319 with Oolite's per-burst particle counts (29 and 14 at r=72.7), which Wegolite does not take (10 per cloud) — disclosed in 20-10, but the wording should be separated; (e) Oolite's bursts inherit the dead ship's velocity (small 1x at OOParticleSystem.m:283, big 0.85x at 324) and Wegolite's are stationary, disclosed in 20-10 but not in the DIV-7 moving-layers list."}]} 
