194:    Per D-01. In `src/app/session/render-driver.ts` export `GAME_OVER_FADE_SECONDS = 5` (doc: Oolite's `gameover-seconds-to-bw-fadeout` default, `PlayerEntity.m:3566-3568` at the pin) and `DEAD_CAMERA_SETBACK_M = 100` (`moveForward:100.0` in `getDestroyedBy:`). In `renderFrame`, beside the `inFlight` camera branch, add a branch for `currentState.mode === "dead"` that uses `computeViewCamera` with the pose position moved `DEAD_CAMERA_SETBACK_M` along the ship's local forward (-Z rotated by the orientation), the pose orientation, `"aft"` and a zero shake, keeping the player's hull hidden as in flight. On the first frame that draws a dead state, clear `ctx.core.previousCameraWorld` before the dust update, so the 100 m camera move gives the dust a zero delta (review round 1, Fable; the warm Load does the same). Compute one effect time `currentState.flightTime + ctx.runtime.gameOverSeconds` and pass it to `shots.update` and `explosions.update` in place of `currentState.flightTime` (alive both values are equal because `gameOverSeconds` is 0); leave the `debris.update` call to Task 2 (D-01c), which moves it to the same effect time and drifts the pieces. Make `hudHidden` true for `"dead"` and toggle `data-dead` on the HUD canvas with `toggleAttribute`, next to the `data-launching` toggle. Write `renderer.domElement.style.filter` as `saturate(<s>)` with `s = 1 - Math.min(1, gameOverSeconds / GAME_OVER_FADE_SECONDS)` while dead and `""` otherwise, and pass the same string to `ctx.runtime.gameOverOverlay?.setFilter` so the game-over text fades with the scene (Oolite fades the whole frame, `PlayerEntity.m:3566-3590`); keep the last written string in the driver, initialised as unknown so the driver's first frame always writes (a reused canvas never keeps a stale filter, review round 1, Kimi), and afterwards write only when it changes. In `shouldDraw`, keep drawing while `ctx.runtime.gameOver` and `gameOverSeconds` is below the settle time (the larger of `GAME_OVER_FADE_SECONDS`, `SMALL_BURST_DURATION` and `BIG_BURST_DURATION`, the two imported from `src/render/bodies/explosions.ts`: since D-01a the player's bursts take their lifetimes from their kind, not from `PLAYER_EXPLOSION_SETTINGS.duration`, and they do not depend on NPC traffic, so neither does the settle time), and treat a settled dead view like a paused one (Task 2 adds the moving-debris exception). Add the behaviour above to `tests/app/session/render-driver.test.ts` with its existing doubles. In the same commit (D-15, AGENTS.md same-commit rule), extend 20-07's game-over entry under `## [Unreleased]` / `### Added` in `CHANGELOG.md` with one sentence placed before its "Press Space or click" sentence: "The view turns to look back at your ship as it explodes, the HUD disappears, and the picture fades to black and white over five seconds." Edit no other entry, no released section, and no version.
